<title>THAILAND: Thai Government Housing Bank to issue 8-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Thai Government Housing Bank to issue 8-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's state-run Government Housing Bank will on Monday issue three billion baht worth of eight-year bonds, a bank official said.  </p>
<p>The bond offered an interest rate of 9.45 percent per annum, to be paid twice a year, the official said.</p>
<p>The proceeds will be used by the bank for loan extensions to individuals wanting to buy a house or apartment.</p>
<p>Tisco Investment and Securities Plc was chosen a the lead underwriter.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
